dots branding patch
Upstream base: egoist/lorca 9033c17710c5d4711a542bf28d2adf756e745af2

Apply only when building dots, preferably in a separate checkout:
  git worktree add --detach ../lorca-dots HEAD
  cd ../lorca-dots
  git apply --check brand.patch
  git apply brand.patch
  bun run build

Undo with: git apply --reverse brand.patch
After syncing upstream, run --check again; review conflicts rather than forcing application.
The Mac release workflow applies this patch automatically before building dots.
Other workflows do not apply it. All other unpatched files follow upstream.
The patch changes display names, executable names/lookup, and the default MCP path
(~/.dots/mcp.json). Explicit alternate data homes retain their own mcp.json.
Other identity/data paths, protocols, dependencies, architectures, access policies,
update enablement, signing keys and upstream endpoints remain unchanged.
The upstream update/install services still provide upstream-branded releases;
installing those can restore upstream branding. No old user files are migrated.
The application release workflows retain upstream signing/publishing requirements;
applying this patch does not grant credentials or turn them into build-only jobs.

