diff --git a/docs/architecture/mcp-servers.md b/docs/architecture/mcp-servers.md
index 196dac0b4395e57c9bae08f0d1990472cc4f3b08..b8e91a23027ad97db63beb52cd6e6cf5ca4ecad0 100644
--- a/docs/architecture/mcp-servers.md
+++ b/docs/architecture/mcp-servers.md
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # MCP servers
 
-The MCP servers the user adds themselves, beside the marketplace's [plugins](plugins.md#plugins), live in `mcp.json` in the CLI's data directory (`crates/cli/src/plugins/mcp_json.rs`), in the format Claude Desktop, Cursor, and Claude Code share: `{ "mcpServers": { "<name>": { … } } }`, each a command (`command`, `args`, `env`, `cwd`) or a remote server (`type` `http`, `url`, `headers`), with `description`, `disabled`, `timeout`, pi's `toolExposure` and `exposure`, and `oauth` (`false`, or how it signs in, below).
+The MCP servers the user adds themselves, beside the marketplace's [plugins](plugins.md#plugins), live in `~/.dots/mcp.json` (`Config::mcp_path`, consumed by `crates/cli/src/plugins/mcp_json.rs`). An alternate data home set through `--home` or `LORCA_HOME` keeps its own `mcp.json`; identity, credentials, and the rest of the default data stay in `~/.lorca`. The file is in the format Claude Desktop, Cursor, and Claude Code share: `{ "mcpServers": { "<name>": { … } } }`, each a command (`command`, `args`, `env`, `cwd`) or a remote server (`type` `http`, `url`, `headers`), with `description`, `disabled`, `timeout`, pi's `toolExposure` and `exposure`, and `oauth` (`false`, or how it signs in, below).
 
 `timeout` is how long a call may go without an answer or progress: seconds, as pi writes it, or milliseconds when it is 1000 or more, as Gemini CLI writes it; ten minutes when unset (`ServerSpec::call_timeout`). `toolExposure` names tools, or patterns ending in `*`, `hidden` or shown (`codemode`, `deferred`, and `direct` all show one, since Lorca's bots reach every plugin tool from a script), and an `exposure` of `hidden` hides every tool not named: an exact name decides first, then the first pattern that matches (`ToolHints::hides`).
 
